.", "options": ["taking", "take", "to take", "takes"], "q": "He admitted ___ the money."}, {"answer": 1, "explanation": "After 'manage', use the to-infinitive.", "options": ["solving", "to solve", "solve", "solves"], "q": "They managed ___ the problem."}, {"answer": 2, "explanation": "After 'enjoy', use the gerund: 'enjoyed travelling'.", "options": ["She suggested leaving early.", "He decided to leave early.", "They enjoyed to travel together.", "We finished eating at nine."], "q": "Which sentence is WRONG?"}, {"answer": 3, "explanation": "After 'afford', use the to-infinitive.", "options": ["buying", "buy", "to buying", "to buy"], "q": "I can't afford ___ a new phone."}, {"answer": 0, "explanation": "After 'avoid', use the gerund.", "options": ["swimming", "swim", "to swim", "swims"], "q": "Avoid ___ in this river — it's dangerous."}, {"answer": 1, "explanation": "After 'offer', use the to-infinitive.", "options": ["helping", "to help", "help", "helps"], "q": "She offered ___ me with my bags."}, {"answer": 2, "explanation": "After 'suggest', use the gerund, never the infinitive.", "options": ["He suggested to go home.", "He suggested go home.", "He suggested going home.", "He suggested to going home."], "q": "Which of the following sentences is correct?"}, {"answer": 3, "explanation": "After 'plan', use the to-infinitive.", "options": ["leaving", "leave", "to leaving", "to leave"], "q": "We planned ___ early."}], "slug": "gerund-vs-infinitive-basic-patterns", "topic": "Gerund vs infinitive (basic patterns)"}